From 95b2aab0ccabe98efe5b9ff5e41ccc4faa609947 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Konstantin Pereiaslov <perk11@perk11.info>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 06:34:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/12] wasm: io barriers - stop the recurring ROM-device
 io_recompile unwind

Why: after the SVC-exit patch the largest remaining
__emscripten_throw_longjmp source was cpu_io_recompile()'s
cpu_loop_exit().  The stock-icount skip kept the rewind for ROM-device
(flash command) accesses because the boot ROM's program/verify
handshake needs the clock-precise 1-insn TB it produces - but the
unsplit TB stays cached, so the firmware's ~7k/s flash status-poll
loop re-pays the ~15-17 us JS-exception unwind on every iteration
(counter ioRewind: 1.67k/s; wprof: ~2.8% of vCPU).

Fix: when io_recompile rewinds, remember the faulting insn (a small
direct-mapped set of 64 guest PCs) and invalidate the offending TB.
The translator keeps barrier insns in single-insn TBs of their own
(stop before one mid-TB, stop after one at TB start): can_do_io is
true throughout a 1-insn TB, so the access completes without
rewinding, with exactly the clock precision the stock rewind produced
- but no further unwinding, ever.  Non-idempotent flash commands are
never double-executed (the stock rewind semantics are kept for the one
occurrence that records the barrier).

Counters after: ioRewind 1.67k/s -> ~0 (one rewind per barrier pc),
tbFlush 0, no >>EXIT<<.  Measured (interleaved A/B vs the previous
build, bootbench window s / finalV / insns @110 s):
  prev  : 27.5 / 154.2 / 1738M   25.3 / 163.7 / 1784M   25.5 / 164.0 / 1818M
  +this : 24.8 / 163.5 / 1756M   25.2 / 164.4 / 1871M   25.2 / 164.4 / 1872M
Candidate wins every pair on all three metrics (+3-5% insns @110 s;
the window improvement is mostly visible when the host is loaded).

Correctness: soak v=373 @330 s, keypad works, native suite PASS x4
(s75/el71/c81/ke800).

Assisted-by: GLM-5.3
